      "value": "@{60285ca04963ba22994f485b|full_name} Since the tracking data and human body bones have always been inconsistent between remote and local clients and for different avatars, and we now have fallback avatar IK syncing to remote clients with some kind of normalized bone rotations for the human body bones, hopefully we're in a good position to bring some consistency to this API. If the rotations used for displaying remote fallback avatars and stuff can be calculated both locally and remotely and then provided as the rotations in udon that wouldn't be a breaking change to the API and then we would have useful body bone rotations and it would be simple to fix tracking data orientations for the remote clients hands as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "6445e3e55dedea0915e4aaeb",
      "author": {
