      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6010b37283e56405c64a79b3|full_name}: applying muscle data to a standardized rig is a lot to ask if you do it every frame for every player because you're just duplicating the amount of work, which is already quite expensive.\n\nBut only doing that once on calibration and saving the difference is a very good idea. It would completely avoid the issue of people having A or I poses, while also providing a much more \"normal\" standard rather than something homebrewed. I'll have to experiment with that some time to see if it would work.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
